> **Purpose / Para que serve:** Global rule applied in every Cursor conversation.
> **Function / Função:** Language policy, security, scope, commit conventions, and edit limits (template).

# Agent Behavior

## Language

- **Canonical docs & rules (this file, `docs/`, `CLAUDE.md`):** EN-US for new and updated content
- **PT-BR:** Supported via `.pt-BR.md` translations — see [docs/I18N_WORKFLOW.md](../../docs/I18N_WORKFLOW.md)
- **User communication:** Match the user's language (PT-BR or EN-US); if unclear, default to EN-US
- **Code, docstrings, and commits:** English always

## Security
- Never hardcode credentials, tokens, or passwords
- Use `config.env` / `config.py` (pydantic-settings) — no literals in versioned code
- Do not commit `.env`, `config.env`, `mcp.env`, or files with real secrets
- Sanitize LDAP/external inputs before filters or queries
- Rate limiting required on new authentication endpoints

## Scope
- Read a file before editing it
- Do not expand scope beyond what was requested
- Tasks touching 5+ files: create a plan in `.cursor/plans/`

## Standards
- Reuse existing patterns in the repository
- Commits: Conventional Commits
- Branches: `feature/<name>` or `fix/<name>`
- Every new API endpoint needs at least one test covering success, 401, and 422

## Git
- Scope: current workspace only
- No force push to `main`/`master` without explicit confirmation
